Coat Rack was very underwhelming when it was released in '''Beta 30.0'''. A 3/5 for 5G that lets you draw 2 cards is very good, but both these cards would increase their cost by 2, making it technically a 3/5 that draws 2 cards for 9G.

This was unusable, so '''Beta 31.0''' gave it a huge buff. While its own cost was increased to 6G, drawn spells won't increase in cost at all. And drawn monsters not only were only given a +1 in cost, they also gain +1 ATK and HP as well, similar to [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Final_Froggit Final Froggit].

'''Beta 50.0''' gave +1/+1 to Coat Rack itself, buffing it to 4/6.

